# Night Ops engineering context

The approved September 2026 plan replaces the previous single-console/no-auth assumptions. Read README.md, STRUCTURE.md, docs/IMPLEMENTATION-CONTRACT.md and docs/DESIGN.md.

Two separately installed Windows products share React playback and a Python media service. Red Lotus Player uses Concept A; Walkman Bridge — Night Ops uses Concept C. Only Bridge loads/bundles device modules, Java and JSymphonic. Each has independent application-data state, cache, queue and SQLite history.

Hard invariants:
- JSymphonic HeadlessCli is the only OMGAUDIO writer. Serialize backup, read, add and delete in the operation coordinator, preserving the private Java lock.
- Bind admitted device work to Windows volume identity; require current ETag for delete. Publish backups only after verification. Unknown writes require reconciliation and never automatic retry.
- Mandatory explicit Defender clearance precedes every decoder and consumer. No production scan bypass or arbitrary scanner executable override. Generated bytes need clearance too.
- App and backend stay unprivileged. Only the narrow packaged helper elevates for fixed scan commands; authenticate IPC and bind OS process identity, nonce, file ID, hash and size.
- Preserve source quality. Playback compatibility uses lossless FLAC; transfer uses separate 192 kbps/44.1 kHz stereo MP3. Web Audio enhancement affects playback only and defaults off.
- Originals are never deleted. Managed-cache leases span processing and playback. Persist structured outcomes and restore sessions paused.
- Enforce exact origin/host, per-launch authentication, CSP, outbound origin restriction and IPC sender validation. Internal scanner/lifecycle routes are native-only.
- Stop/release playback before draining all admitted work. Unknown status is never idle; no automatic timeout kills device writes.
- Preserve existing dirty work and terminal job history. No publication is implied by building installers.

Use functional React and existing modules rather than adding a state framework or another device engine. Keep frontend requests in api.js. Use the official outlined lotus, local Orbitron/Plex fonts, maroon/ember colors, visible focus, readable responsive layouts and reduced motion. Do not execute the exported HTML wrapper, external loaders or fixture data.

Run meaningful regression and integration checks and obtain independent correctness/security review. Test mocks never weaken production clearance. Physical NW-S705F verification requires an operator-controlled test after a full backup; do not claim mock success proves firmware playback.
